- Constraints to consider: depot capacities, unit demands, per-unit supply volumes, vehicle capacity, and the limit on total deployed vehicles. A route must be activated to use any associated vehicles; activating a route incurs a fixed risk cost regardless of vehicle count (escort/security overhead, route clearance), which must be included in the objective.
- Approach: optimize flows from depots to units across active routes to satisfy demand with minimum combined costs and penalties, while respecting route activation limits and fleet size. Favor strategies that meet critical demands with low-cost routes and minimize unused capacity (slack) where feasible.
